[O][A Shaman] On the notice board beside the town hall, [QA95999 WANTED: Incinerator Gar'im] (|cFFFF0000GROUP 2+|r, a level 23 elite at the Blackrock camp in the south-east corner, 25 units south of the falls; taken for the boots only - see the gear line) [G24.4,46.2 Redridge Mountains]
[A Shaman] Take the road east along the north shore, past the watch tower beside Stonewatch Keep (58.2,49.8), to the Old Lion Statue [G79.4,46.8 Redridge Mountains]
[A Shaman] Walk south to the foot of Stonewatch Falls beside the Murloc Nightcrawlers (level 21-22) and use the [UI265747 Unfilled Red Waterskin] there [QC94499] [G76.1,59.6 Redridge Mountains]
[OC][A Shaman] The DB has no object for the falls; the quest text puts it near the Nightcrawlers, whose only spawns are here. Rohh the Silent (a level 26 rare) also has spawn points in this corner - leave him
[O][A Shaman] |cFFFF0000GROUP 2+|r Carry on south down the east edge to the corner of the zone and kill [TAR214519 Incinerator Gar'im] for the Broken Staff - a level 23 elite, five or six levels under you, who wanders the camp: the DB has 122 positions for him between 67-73,79-87, so look around the middle of that patch (the Grunts and Outrunners around him are 19-21) [QC95999] [G71.5,84.3 Redridge Mountains]
[O][A Shaman] Back in Lakeshire at [TAR344 Magistrate Solomon], [QT95999] (2,550 XP) [G24.9,44.5 Redridge Mountains]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear (Gar'im):|r Disjointed Shoes - leather, +12 Attack Power and +5 spell damage: take them. Alacritous Treads are mail (+5 Str +5 Agi) and Incinerator's Boots cloth (+3 Sta +6 Int): pass
[A Shaman] At [TAR931 Ariena Stormfeather] in Lakeshire, |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Thelsamar]|r (the game routes it through Stormwind and Ironforge) [G25.5,59.4 Redridge Mountains]

[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffWetlands: Hervdana, first visit|r  -  Dun Algaz (Dragonmaw orcs, level 19-21), then east to the cave under the southern falls. |cffffcc00Golm|r, a level 32 ELITE elemental: the DB (QuestieDB 1.1.1) lists 79 positions for him, 46 of them inside x64-69, y66-75.5 - the nearest is one unit north of the cave mouth. The quest that kills him wakes him with a Goaz Stone, so he may stand dormant until then (unverified). Look before you cross the last stretch, come in from the south-west along the south edge, and if he is up and close to the door, wait until he has moved north
[A Shaman] From Thelsamar run up the west road to the north exit at Mountaineer Rockgar [G25.4,10.4 Loch Modan]
[A Shaman] Through Dun Algaz to where the pass opens into the Wetlands [G48.6,76.0 Wetlands]
